matrix-overlay (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Upstream 0.1.2: the release process and the distribution channel are now one
    command (packaging/publish.sh / "make publish"), and adding our repository
    is
    one file for a client thanks to the matrix-overlay-repo configuration
    package (key + deb822 source entry, both conffiles).
  * publish_repo.sh accepts repeated --deb and indexes the whole pool, so the
    application and its repository configuration ship in one signed repository;
    component-to-package ownership is derived per package instead of assumed.
  * Packaging review pass: source format 3.0 (quilt), debian/watch,
    debian/upstream/metadata, Standards-Version 4.7.4, one Priority declaration
    in the source stanza, and an autopkgtest over the installed package.
  * Tests: 375 green, including guards that the shipped key is public-only and
    that the autopkgtest stays display-free and network-free.

 -- Nelson Pascoal <foomip@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:05:00 +0200

matrix-overlay (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Source format: "3.0 (native)" is not a valid dpkg-source format string -
    native is "1.0 (native)". Switched to 3.0 (quilt), which is what the archive
    expects for a package whose tarball comes from an upstream tag.
  * debian/watch: follow the GitHub tags (pgpmode=none while the tags are
    unsigned). debian/upstream/metadata records the repository, the bug tracker
    and the changelog URL.
    * Standards-Version 4.7.4. Priority is declared once, in the source stanza,
  and
    inherited by the binary package: Policy 4.7.3 no longer requires the field,
    but dpkg-genchanges in Ubuntu 24.04 still warns and emits "Priority: -" when
    nothing declares it (cf. Debian #1124443).
  * debian/tests: two autopkgtests. "unit" runs the 370-case suite from the
    source tree (it is headless by design: no compositor is needed), "installed"
    exercises the shipped command the way a user would without drawing anything
    on screen (--help, --preflight, and the binary-hardening assertions).

 -- Nelson Pascoal <foomip@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:58:37 +0200

matrix-overlay (0.1.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Store metadata now survives AppStream processing: the icon SVG parses under
    gdk-pixbuf (no comments before the root element), media URLs no longer rely
    on redirects, and the component category is one AppStream accepts. Broken
    any of these, and appstream-compose drops the component from the catalogue
    without saying so.
  * Published as a signed apt repository (packaging/publish_repo.sh): the
    repository now ships the DEP-11 catalogue with a Package link, so COSMIC
    Store can install the app rather than merely describe it.
  * Documentation: the packaging rules that were measured on a client (catalogue
    path, three compressed forms, Origin header, Package link), the render-node
    selection ladder, and why the store route is native and not Flatpak.

 -- Nelson Pascoal <foomip@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 17:12:00 +0200

matrix-overlay (0.1.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * First packaged release: GPU-composited Matrix rain over every output on
    COSMIC/Wayland, triggered by a custom shortcut (Ctrl+Shift+M by convention).
  * The render node and EGL vendor are detected from the connectors that are
    actually driven, so one package serves hybrid and single-GPU machines.
  * Config chain: --config, MATRIX_OVERLAY_CONFIG, ~/.config, then
    /etc/matrix-overlay/config.toml (installed here as a conffile).
  * Cairo/GTK layer-shell painting remains as a fallback for compositors whose
    GL path is unusable; it is a Recommends, not a Depends.

 -- Nelson Pascoal <foomip@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 13:19:48 +0200
